{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-105663-r4518928","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pulikkachal (Tamil Spiced Tamarind Paste)","sourcePageId":105663,"sourceRevision":"4518928","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:19:03Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pulikkachal%20(Tamil%20Spiced%20Tamarind%20Paste)&oldid=4518928","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:08.534Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dal recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using chickpea","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using fenugreek seed","Category:Recipes using tamarind","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"f3a7ddb534d8e626e1e9f7dcd48ee6342324f669983d397e776f9abc7be849e7","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Condiment recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''''Pulikkachal''''', alternately spelled ''pulikachal'', is a spiced [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] paste. It is commonly mixed with rice to make tamarind rice (''Puliyodharai'').\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seeds (dhaniya)\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Fenugreek|fenugreek]] seeds\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Sesame Seed|sesame seeds]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Urad Bean|urad]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dhal]] (black gram)\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Chickpea|channa]] dhal (split chick-peas)\n*4 red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] extract\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]]\n\n* [[Cookbook:Peanut|Peanuts]] (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n# [[Cookbook:Roasting|Roast]] the coriander, fenugreek, and sesame seeds without oil. Grind into fine powder.\n# Heat oil in a pan and add urad dhal, chickpeas and red chilies and [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] for a few minutes. Add tamarind extract and salt. Allow it to [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Add the ground spice powder and asafoetida, and mix well.\n#Stir constantly until it becomes thick and the oil floats on the top of the mixture and it comes without sticking to the pan. Refrigerate and store.\n# You can mix this with cooked rice and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tamarind]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fenugreek seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pulikkachal (Tamil Spiced Tamarind Paste)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tsp coriander seeds (dhaniya)","sourceText":"1 tsp coriander seeds (dhaniya)","amountText":"1 tsp coriander seeds (dhaniya)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tsp fenugreek seeds","sourceText":"1 tsp fenugreek seeds","amountText":"1 tsp fenugreek seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","na